  "question": {
    "text": "If the system of linear equations\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x+a y+z=3 \\\\\n&x+2 y+2 z=6 \\\\\n&x+5 y+3 z=b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nhas no solution, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Yrb9i",
      "text": "\n$a=1, b \\neq 9$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TR6Zc",
      "text": "\n$a \\neq-1, b=9$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RmHgO",
      "text": "\n$a=-1, b=9$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qiJtF",
      "text": "\n$a=-1, b \\neq 9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As the system of equations has no solution then $\\Delta$ should be zero and at least one of $\\Delta_1$, $\\Delta_2$ and $\\Delta_3$ should not be zero.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\therefore \\Delta=\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\n1 & a & 1 \\\\\n1 & 2 & 2 \\\\\n1 & 5 & 3\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow-a-1=0 \\Rightarrow a=-1 \\\\\n&\\Delta_2=\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\n1 & 3 & 1 \\\\\n1 & 6 & 2 \\\\\n1 & b & 3\n\\end{array}\\right| \\neq 0 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow b \\neq 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
